WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.434
-I wanted to ask you because you
have something

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.767
in common with
Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.801
He actually wrote an episode of
"Veronica Mars"?

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.334
-He did.
We're marshmallows, guys.

00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:10.734
He's a marshmallow.
-Really?

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:12.634
-Yes.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.767
He is a spectacular writer.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.701
For anyone who hasn't read
anything he's written,

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.834
I highly, highly recommend you
seek it out.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.133
He's got such
a great perspective,

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.601
he's such an awesome writer.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:26.100
And during the reboot at Hulu,
he, like, submitted to be

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.601
a writer and Rob Thomas,
our creator, like, freaked out.

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.100
-Yeah, like, "Wait, Kareem
watches 'Veronica Mars'?

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.133
He likes us?"
-We were like, "what?"

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.701
And he wrote
a spectacular episode.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.267
So we worked together.
-How cool is that?

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:39.067
I love that.
-Pretty cool.

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:41.133
-I want to get to the book.
Congrats on this.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.334
-Thank you.
-It's awesome.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:47.200
This weekend was Father's Day,
and I know Dax,

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:49.734
your husband, Dax Shepard,
very, very funny individual.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.400
I love him.
-Yeah. He's a stud.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.434
-He's a stud.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:53.701
-He's funny,
but he's also a stud.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:56.167
-He is a stud.
-Yeah.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:59.067
-When I knew him, he was always
in shape, but now he's jacked.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:02.133
-He is -- He took COVID
very seriously.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.534
-Yeah.
-Yeah. He was --

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.567
-He took it as an opportunity
to just lift.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.033
-Lift so much.
-Yeah.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.534
-He lifts all the time.
He loves muscles.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.300
It's really cute.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.534
-But he has his own gym, right?
-He has his own gym.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.901
And that's -- what's funny --
well, ironic, is he was

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.167
out of town for Mother's Day,

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.734
and I was out of town
for Father's Day,

00:01:19.734 --> 00:01:21.000
so we kind of blew it.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.067
But on Saturday we got him
out of the house.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:25.767
His buddy, like, took him
somewhere.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:29.434
And my girls and I -- He has
a gym, which is our garage.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:32.167
And it is not new.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:36.534
And he calls it Black Mold
Paradise because he has,

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:39.267
for about the last year
and a half, been challenging

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:42.901
The Rock publicly to, like,
I guess workout battles?

00:01:42.901 --> 00:01:44.601
[ Laughter ]
-Is that a thing?

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.634
-I guess.
Like, lifting challenges maybe?

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.467
It's not like a fight.

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.334
He's not dumb. He doesn't want
to fight The Rock.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:55.167
He posts on Instagram a lot
like, "Bring it on, Dwayne."

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:58.234
Because he has Iron Paradise,
which is this beautiful gym.

00:01:58.234 --> 00:02:00.234
-Oh, The Rock's gym is
unbelievable.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.868
And he doesn't let anyone work
out there.

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:03.033
-He doesn't?
-No, no, it's, like, secret.

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:05.033
-Oh, then this is
a losing battle for Dax.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.167
Well, I think what Dax is trying
to do is invite him

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.767
to Black Mold Paradise, which is
about the size of this stage.

00:02:09.767 --> 00:02:11.801
-Black Mold Paradise?
-Black Mold Paradise, yeah.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.000
'Cause there's a little --

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.334
There's some creepy crawlies
in the corners.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.901
-Yeah, there's something growing
in there.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:19.968
-But what he calls it --
his full name for the gym is

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:22.501
Dan Gainz -- with a Z --

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:27.567
Dan Gainz Beef Haus
#blackmoldparadise.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:30.834
By the way, he uses this hashtag
on Instagram all the time.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.100
-And it makes no sense. No one
knows what he's talking about.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.067
-Nobody knows what it is.
He doesn't care.

00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:35.534
-He doesn't care.
-No, he doesn't care.

00:02:35.534 --> 00:02:38.100
-Dan Gainz --
-Dan Gainz -- he calls himself

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.634
Dan for, like, takeout 'cause
nobody knows what Dax is.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.567
-Yeah, they don't recognize that
as a name.

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.067
-Right, and they're like,
"Sure, Zack."

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:47.033
And he's like,
"I'll just say Dan."

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.868
Dan Gainz Beef Haus
#blackmoldparadise.

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.501
So for Father's Day, we got him
out of the house.

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:55.501
And my girls and I went in there
and we spray-painted

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:58.234
Dan Gainz Beef Haus
#blackmoldparadise.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:01.167
And, like, decorated with
acrylic markers all over

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:04.100
the inside of his gym to cover
up all the black mold.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.534
-Here's a picture right here.

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.334
-Yeah.
-Dan Gainz Beef Haus.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.234
-Beef Haus.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.834
-It almost seems like German.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:17.234
-So, I got, like,
vinyl stencils.

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.434
That's the cool thing about
knowing prop masters

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:20.667
from, like, film and TV work.
-Yeah, we're lucky.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.334
-You can be like,
"Can I get a vinyl stencil,

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.767
like 12 inches by 9 feet?"

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.334
And they're like, "Absolutely."

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:28.133
-I want to see, like --
He should make hot dogs.

00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.000
-I'm sure he would not have
a problem with it.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.434
-[ German accent ] Beef Haus.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.701
-When I met him, he had
a hot dog maker that was like

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.167
half the size of this table,
like, in the kitchen.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.534
-And I was like --

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:40.267
-Dax, I will -- I will take that
from you, Dax.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.567
-We've already given it away.
-You already gave it away?

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:43.634
-Yeah, we gave it to
Ryan Hansen.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:44.834
It still comes out
once in a while,

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.133
but it's not in my kitchen.

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:47.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.801
-I have some things, where,
yeah, my wife was like,

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.334
"Yeah, we're good with that
if you want to give it

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.767
to your friend or something."

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.400
Why don't you want
this wall-sized poster

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.067
of the Beastie Boys?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.067 --> 00:03:58.000
"It's time to move on, bud."

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.100
-Sometimes you just gotta --
-Yeah.

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.934
My buddy gave me this thing
I still have in my office.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.434
He was like --
'Cause I love Buddy Holly.

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:06.801
It's just a weird two things.

00:04:06.801 --> 00:04:09.100
I love Buddy Holly,
and I also love stained glass.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.701
-Okay.
-And I don't know why it just

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.267
came up, and he's like,
"You love stained glass."

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:14.801
And he said something like,
"Do you like Buddy Holly?"

00:04:14.801 --> 00:04:16.200
And I go, "I do actually."

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.968
He goes, "I have a stained-Glass
portrait of Buddy Holly..."

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:20.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.067
"...that my wife is like,
'there's no way we're

00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:23.634
keeping this
in the living room.'"

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:25.100
So I go, "I will borrow it,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:28.100
and whenever you need it back,
I will hang it in my office."

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:29.601
And it's been in my office
since "Late Night."

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.834
Neal Brennan, if you need it
back, I have it.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:34.767
-Oh, my God.
Neal, you got rid of that?

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:36.868
-No, yeah, it's pretty --
It's pretty magical, yeah.

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:39.033
-That's amazing. Sometimes you
inherit some good stuff.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.167
-Yeah, I like it.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:41.767
I want to talk about
your new book.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:43.467
Congrats on this, by the way.
-Thank you.

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.801
-"The World Needs
More Purple Schools."

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:48.434
-Out tomorrow.
Your first book,

00:04:48.434 --> 00:04:50.634
"The World Needs
More Purple People,"

00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:52.868
was an instant "New York Times"
best seller.

00:04:52.868 --> 00:04:54.334
Right to number one.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:56.133
Congrats on that.
-Thank you.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:58.634
-It's great. I love the art.

00:04:58.634 --> 00:05:01.501
I love the --
I love all of the, uh --

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.634
-There's a lot of boogers in it.
-There's boogers in it?

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:04.801
-There was boogers
in the first one.

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.601
There's boogers
in this one, guys.

00:05:06.601 --> 00:05:09.868
-Yeah, it'll make kids laugh
and kids happy and make --

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:12.667
-Hopefully better people too.
Hopefully good people.

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.100
-It'll make people think
and make good people,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.167
which is what we want.
That's the point.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.567
-That was kind of the goal.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.467 --> 00:05:19.834
-That's the point.
-That's the point.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:21.934
Well, 'cause, yeah, in the first
one, we identified these

00:05:21.934 --> 00:05:24.801
five principles we thought
were -- it was like, we wrote

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.534
the first one when the world was
arguing.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:28.901
Remember when, like, everyone
was arguing about everything,

00:05:28.901 --> 00:05:30.934
and it was the only thing
everybody wanted to do?

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:33.834
It's, like, died down a little
bit, but we still love to argue.

00:05:33.834 --> 00:05:35.601
And so, we were like, "What if
we come up with these

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:40.133
purple principles that made
being nice and responsible

00:05:40.133 --> 00:05:41.434
and a good listener cool?"

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:44.934
So we were like, "purple people,
they ask great questions.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.801
They laugh a lot.
They work hard.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:48.801
They use their voice,
and they listen.

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:51.634
And they -- Just be you.
Because you're the --"

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.801
We like to say, "Because you're
the only you we've got."

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.400
-Yeah, that is true.
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:58.000
[ Applause ]
I love that.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.067
And there's a little Easter egg
in here,

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:03.033
a tiny nod to "Frozen,"
which I like.

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:04.667
And you're like --
Can we just see there?

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:05.901
In a little -- "Let it go."

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:08.234
-"And then she said,
'Let it go, let it go.'"

00:06:08.234 --> 00:06:10.734
-Yes! Exactly right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:13.667
-And then there's the boogers!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:16.067
-There are boogers there, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:18.467
-Tough segue right into
"Frozen."

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:20.734
-True.
-You know, I love "Frozen II."

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.801
-Thank you.
-I almost liked it

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:25.033
maybe better -- Can I say that?
-Of course you can.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.334
You can say whatever you want.
-That's true, I can.

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:27.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:27.267 --> 00:06:29.067
-It's your show.
-It is my show.

00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:32.834
I did enjoy "Frozen," but
"Frozen II" kind of -- great.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:35.734
"Frozen 3," can we announce
anything?

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:40.434
-I would like
to officially announce --

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:41.968
[ Drumroll ]

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.167
With zero authority,
"Frozen 3."

00:06:45.167 --> 00:06:46.467
-Wow!

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:52.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:55.033
-Please bear in mind I did say
"zero authority"

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:57.133
'cause I can't do that.
-Yeah, you can't announce it.

00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:59.133
-I'm not -- I can't do that.
No, I'm not in charge.

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.501
-But there could be something
maybe in the works

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:02.834
and maybe happening, maybe.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:05.634
-Well, you know, I'm --
I'll keep it mysterious.

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.667
But I know Idina recently said
she would do it,

00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:10.667
And I feel like
if we're all in...

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:11.868
-We're all in.
-What are we waiting for?

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:13.501
-Come on, we want it.
-We want it. Let's do it.

00:07:13.501 --> 00:07:15.400
-Kristen Bell.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.167
"The World Needs
More Purple Schools"

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:20.133
is available tomorrow!

